{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>A hind let loose.</b> This is the valley of Ginosar, whose fruits ripen as swiftly as this hind that runs swiftly. אַיָּלָה שְׁלֻחָה — a hind dispatched to run." "<b>He gives words of beauty.</b> As the Targum renders. Another interpretation: he prophesied concerning the war against Sisera — ״וְלָקַחְתָּ עִמְּךָ עֲשֶׂרֶת אֲלָפִים אִישׁ מִבְּנֵי נַפְתָּלִי וְגוֹ׳״ (Judges 4), and they went there with dispatch; and so the language of שִׁלּוּחַ is used there: ״בָּעֵמֶק שֻׁלַּח בְּרַגְלָיו״." "<b>He gives words of beauty.</b> Through them Deborah and Barak sang song. And our Rabbis expounded it concerning the day of Jacob's burial, when Esau disputed the cave, in tractate Sotah (13a). And its Targum: יִתְרְמֵי עַדְבֵהּ — his portion falls, and he acknowledges his lot with beautiful sayings and praise."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:15.307797291Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}